1. d4 {... etc. "Members and visitors to the Congress re­gretted to hear on
Saturday that Blackburne was indisposed, and would not be able to leave his
hotel. However it was arranged that his game with Mackenzie should be played
in private, and the veteran hopes to be able to take his place again in the
chessroom to-day. The game (queen’s pawn opening) soon resolved itself into
an ending with rook, knight, and four pawns against rook, bishop, and four
pawns, and a draw was the natural result." (Manchester Guardian, 21 August
1905)} 1/2-1/2

