1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 {...etc. Not quite clear whether a draw was agreed
in this game. According to the Manchester Guardian, 26 Aug 1905, "the game
between the two last was left unfinished". The newspaper then gives the
players' scores as Gunston 2.5 and Shoosmith 2. "The most determined fight of
the day to avoid the draw took place between Gunston and Shoosmith. After
twenty-five moves not a single piece was off the board. After another twenty
moves one pawn had been exchanged, and the doughty combatants were at a late
hour in solo possession of the room, every other game having been finished."}
1/2-1/2

